# Three-layer schema unit tests in SchemaTest.cpp; no gtest, as its header explains the user
# decision.
# RUN: spinel-spbpf-schema-test %S/schema-roundtrip.json | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: ok   fixture parses
# Types: nested structs are named record references, not anonymous copies.
# CHECK: ok   core: a nested struct is a record_ref, not an anonymous copy
# CHECK: ok   core: char[16] is an array type
# CHECK: ok   core: record_ref size resolves through the schema
# Ring buffers remain in schema without requiring key/value on every map.
# CHECK: ok   core: a ringbuf map has no key/value and names its record
# Telemetry carries AST rather than prose.
# CHECK: ok   telemetry: drop predicate survives as an AST
# CHECK: ok   telemetry: semconv key and stability survive
# CHECK: ok   telemetry: what cannot be expressed goes to runtime_extension, not silently dropped
# logs body / metrics value / closed metric kinds (sum, exponential_histogram)
# CHECK: ok   telemetry: sum keeps its declared monotonic
# CHECK: ok   telemetry: a logs body source survives
# CHECK: ok   telemetry: exponential_histogram keeps scale / zero_threshold / bucket_rule
# Core preserves extensions without interpreting them.
# CHECK: ok   extensions: spinel.ebpf is preserved verbatim (core does not read it)
# CHECK: ok   decode(encode(x)) == x
# CHECK: ok   encode is idempotent (canonical)
# CHECK: ok   extension payload survives a parse/serialize round trip
# CHECK: ok   accepts coverage.programs = omitted (a partial schema)
# CHECK: schema-unittest: 81/81 checks passed
